## Exam Importance & Requirements

- **Domain**: Cluster Maintenance & Troubleshooting (Killer.sh Question 22).
- **Exam Pattern**: *"Check the expiration date of all certificates on the control plane. Identify when the API server
  certificate expires using both kubeadm and OpenSSL. Renew the API server certificate without disturbing the cluster."*
- **Key Concepts**:
  1. `kubeadm certs check-expiration` checks all certificates in `/etc/kubernetes/pki` and embedded client certificates
     in `/etc/kubernetes/*.conf`.
  1. OpenSSL direct inspection: `openssl x509 -in /etc/kubernetes/pki/apiserver.crt -noout -dates` validates the on-disk
     x509 certificate.
  1. Component-specific renewal: `kubeadm certs renew apiserver` regenerates the certificate while retaining the
     existing private key and CA authority.
  1. Service disruption prevention: After renewal, static pod containers (`kube-apiserver`) automatically reload or can
     be restarted via `crictl` without re-initializing the cluster.

